WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:19.580
<b>Here to perform their new song, "lovely weather."
The Sunflower Dolls</b>

00:01.500 --> 00:06.500
So I hear you'll be going around CD shops
nationwide starting today?

00:06.500 --> 00:10.460
Yes! This is our comeback,
so we want to go back to our roots first.

00:10.710 --> 00:14.630
We're going to do everything we did back
when we came out with our debut single.

00:14.920 --> 00:16.880
Or so the grownups told you to do.

00:16.880 --> 00:18.580
Oh, come on!

00:19.630 --> 00:21.380
To close, here's an announcement.

00:21.380 --> 00:22.880
Take it away, Mero.

00:24.500 --> 00:27.670
Thank you! The Sunflower Dolls are making a comeback!

00:27.670 --> 00:32.540
To kick off, we're releasing a double
A-side single next Wednesday!

00:32.790 --> 00:35.630
This will be the first time in two years that the Sundolls-

00:53.330 --> 00:58.250
Mahou wa itsukara tsukaeru yoni narunoka

00:58.380 --> 01:03.170
Tokubetsu na nanika ni zutto akogareteta

01:03.460 --> 01:08.330
1 2 3 de maenarae B C D iiko ni suru no wa

01:08.460 --> 01:13.920
Watashi janai tte watashi ga ichiban shitteirunda

01:14.790 --> 01:20.500
Konomama de ii nante dare mo omocchanai yo

01:20.500 --> 01:23.290
Aseru ryouashi ga omoi no

01:24.290 --> 01:27.960
Konna ni chikaku ni iru kimi ni sae

01:28.080 --> 01:32.670
Modokashii hodo todokanai noni kono me ga utsushita

01:32.920 --> 01:38.540
Irotoridori yoridori midori no mei

01:38.540 --> 01:43.540
Nando datte mou iyannatatte kimi to kyoumei

01:43.750 --> 01:48.540
Loop shisou na shikou o yabutte

01:48.540 --> 01:53.170
Yuutsu na hibi ni mayday watashi wa chuu o matte

01:53.170 --> 01:57.830
Kumorizora no fuchi ni kaburitsuki

01:58.000 --> 02:05.790
Nomikomu nigai suppai shoppai igai ni amai no kamoshirenai na

02:08.130 --> 02:14.880
Hikari no sashikomu hou e ikunda

02:22.670 --> 02:24.420
Hey, we got 10,000 views!

02:23.460 --> 02:28.080
<b>Episode 4:  Double A-Side</b>

02:26.710 --> 02:29.080
Isn't 10k with our first video pretty decent?

02:29.710 --> 02:31.170
Compared to before, at least.

02:31.880 --> 02:33.040
<b>[MV] "Invincible Girl" / JELEE
JELEE · 10K views</b>

02:32.040 --> 02:34.670
Uh, right...

02:33.330 --> 02:34.830
<b>Me singing a guitar arrangement of "Colorful Moonlight"
by the Sunflower Dolls</b>

02:33.340 --> 02:34.830
<b>JELEE · 132 views</b>

02:35.210 --> 02:36.630
I guess that's true.

02:37.540 --> 02:41.040
By the way, Mei.
Wasn't there something you wanted to ask?

02:41.290 --> 02:46.330
I was practicing this... DTM... thing, but I'm stuck.

02:46.830 --> 02:50.500
Um, I want to create a... "track"?

02:50.710 --> 02:53.250
But I can't find where the "roll" is.

02:54.420 --> 02:55.290
Do you get it, Yoru?

02:55.290 --> 02:57.710
That's was totally some other language.

02:58.290 --> 03:01.710
That's it. We gotta get an interpreter.

03:02.920 --> 03:05.670
Yeah, that's right. Does the sound play now?

03:06.130 --> 03:08.420
Hmm... I got an error.

03:08.670 --> 03:09.750
What does it say?

03:09.750 --> 03:13.420
Uh, something about an "audio driver"?

03:13.710 --> 03:16.130
Maybe there's a screw loose somewhere?

03:16.290 --> 03:18.250
It has nothing to do with a screwdriver.

03:19.960 --> 03:21.670
Hey, Kiui.

03:22.290 --> 03:26.540
If it's okay with you,
could you maybe actually come here?

03:26.790 --> 03:30.130
I mean, I haven't even gotten to thank you in person.

03:30.330 --> 03:32.040
Uh, well...

03:32.040 --> 03:33.540
You see, uhh...

03:33.540 --> 03:37.040
Kiui's pretty busy, and I really
don't wanna impose, you know?

03:37.380 --> 03:40.250
Yoru, you're a tad too considerate sometimes.

03:40.250 --> 03:41.750
Hey, your face is too close!

03:41.750 --> 03:43.920
You don't need to be shy around me!

03:44.170 --> 03:45.000
Then how's this?

03:45.000 --> 03:45.630
Hmm?

03:46.290 --> 03:48.670
I'll go if we do it at Kano Yamanouchi's place.

03:49.790 --> 03:50.380
Huh?

03:51.330 --> 03:52.790
<b>Sunflower Dolls</b>

03:52.750 --> 03:52.790
<b>Mero Setou</b>

03:53.040 --> 03:58.580
Seriously though, touring CD shops in this day and age?
Isn't that way too analog?

03:58.750 --> 04:01.170
Remote work is the way to go these days!

04:01.540 --> 04:04.630
But this campaign was Ms. Yukine's idea.

04:04.750 --> 04:12.000
What? Really?! Then there's probably some unfathomable
strategy I couldn't even hope to understand.

04:12.000 --> 04:12.750
Wow!

04:15.380 --> 04:19.330
We appreciate you coming!
We put our hearts into these autographs!

04:20.000 --> 04:23.630
As shop owner, I'll make sure we push
to promote these on the release date.

04:23.830 --> 04:25.830
Thank you so much!

04:25.960 --> 04:29.460
Oh, and... if you don't mind, please take that as well.

04:29.460 --> 04:30.880
<b>Sunflower Dolls</b>

04:29.880 --> 04:33.830
Wow, that's very impressive! But...

04:34.170 --> 04:36.420
I'm not sure we have a place to put it.

04:38.330 --> 04:39.790
Oh, it's Ms. Yukine.

04:39.790 --> 04:40.500
Uh?!

04:41.830 --> 04:42.540
Hello?

04:42.960 --> 04:44.500
Right. No, actually,

04:44.750 --> 04:46.960
he says he might not have a place to put it.

04:47.670 --> 04:48.880
Um, well...

04:49.670 --> 04:51.170
We'll make space.

04:52.000 --> 04:53.960
<b>Shinjuku Station</b>

04:54.580 --> 04:56.210
My idol... My idol...

04:56.380 --> 04:57.540
My idol's home!

04:58.040 --> 05:02.920
It's nothing that great. I just live in
a rundown apartment with my big sister.

05:02.920 --> 05:04.460
Y-you have an older sister?!

05:05.170 --> 05:07.750
Well, she's hardly ever home because of work.

05:08.630 --> 05:09.880
Oh, here she comes.

05:13.540 --> 05:15.790
Hi there! I'm Kano Yamanouchi!

05:16.130 --> 05:18.790
Um, I'm Mei Kim Anouk Takanashi.

05:19.750 --> 05:22.250
Hey. I'm Kiui Watase.

05:25.330 --> 05:27.420
That hair color's amazing!

05:27.420 --> 05:28.080
Huh?

05:29.040 --> 05:32.830
It's lovely! Some pop idols have hair like that these days.

05:35.040 --> 05:36.920
Complimenting me won't get you anything.

05:38.540 --> 05:39.580
What's that supposed to mean?

05:39.580 --> 05:40.670
It's great meeting you.

05:40.960 --> 05:42.830
Yeah. Nice meeting you, too.

05:43.290 --> 05:46.630
But is Tatekita pretty lax about their dress code?

05:46.630 --> 05:48.880
I had this image of black hair and conservative looks.

05:48.880 --> 05:49.710
Well, uh...

05:49.710 --> 05:50.290
Huh?

05:54.670 --> 05:56.750
Sorry, that was a lie.

06:01.670 --> 06:04.920
All that about being popular and
student council president was just tough talk.

06:05.380 --> 06:07.630
I'm not going to school right now.

06:08.080 --> 06:11.330
Huh? Then what we heard from Miss Mahiru...

06:11.790 --> 06:13.420
I made it all up.

06:14.130 --> 06:15.000
Sorry.

06:16.790 --> 06:18.000
Huh.

06:19.710 --> 06:21.250
Then we're the same!

06:21.670 --> 06:22.250
Huh?

06:22.960 --> 06:25.750
I don't go much, either. To school.

06:25.750 --> 06:31.670
Though mine has a lot of students in showbiz,
so it's not that unusual.

06:32.040 --> 06:33.920
Oh... okay.

06:34.750 --> 06:43.290
So basically, JELEE is really well-balanced with two
normal high school girls and two girls avoiding school!

06:44.790 --> 06:47.830
Uh, not sure I'd call that well-balanced.

06:50.210 --> 06:55.040
So anyway, in all seriousness,
what's easiest for you to start off with?

06:54.330 --> 06:56.880
They both seem nice, don't they?

06:55.040 --> 07:00.250
The melody...? Actually, having the lyrics first might
make it easier to come up with a melody.

06:59.250 --> 07:02.080
Well, this beats getting hit on, at least.

07:02.170 --> 07:04.460
Guess I gotta come up with something, then.

07:05.330 --> 07:07.290
Hey, can we stop by there?

07:07.920 --> 07:09.380
Tiramisu cups?

07:09.630 --> 07:10.830
Sounds delicious!

07:11.170 --> 07:13.000
There's a pretty long line, though.

07:13.330 --> 07:15.960
Yeah, Yukochi featured it the other day.

07:16.330 --> 07:18.580
That's the power of 350k followers.

07:18.750 --> 07:19.960
Nope, sorry.

07:19.960 --> 07:22.250
We're not here to enjoy ourselves today, remember?

07:22.750 --> 07:25.880
That's true. Though they do look tasty.

07:28.250 --> 07:30.380
Right... That's too bad.

07:32.000 --> 07:36.080
Amazing! Yukine-pi wins at life, am I right?

07:36.420 --> 07:40.580
Mero, I really think you should stop
adding "pi" to the producer's name.

07:40.580 --> 07:44.750
Huh? Why? Doesn't "P" stand for "producer"?

07:45.040 --> 07:48.750
I don't think anyone else uses
"pi" to mean "producer," though.

07:49.130 --> 07:52.580
But all you did was drop her name. That's amazing.

07:52.880 --> 07:55.830
<b>Sunflower
Dolls</b>

07:53.000 --> 07:55.170
I mean, it's the K Records in Shinjuku!

07:55.960 --> 08:01.040
Mm-hm! That's why we're set as long
as we follow Yukine-pi's lead!

08:01.170 --> 08:06.920
High income! High income! The best recruitment website HANIWA!

08:01.500 --> 08:05.790
You might be right. If we make a comeback
and flop, that's it for us,

08:06.500 --> 08:08.000
for sure this time.

08:08.130 --> 08:13.040
High income! High income! The best recruitment website HANIWA!

08:09.500 --> 08:11.750
After a scandal like that, yeah...

08:13.540 --> 08:16.920
Hey come on, no more gloomy talk!

08:17.460 --> 08:19.580
That's all over and done with.

08:19.580 --> 08:20.790
All right.

08:21.130 --> 08:23.580
Over and done with, huh?

08:25.330 --> 08:26.540
Thanks for having us over.

08:26.830 --> 08:28.170
Th-thanks for having us!

08:28.170 --> 08:29.420
Come on in.

08:30.170 --> 08:31.000
Whoa...

08:32.460 --> 08:33.580
Wow...

08:34.210 --> 08:36.420
This is so the life of a struggling musician.

08:36.420 --> 08:37.830
You'll ruin your health.

08:37.830 --> 08:40.880
What am I supposed to do? I'm no good at cooking.

08:40.880 --> 08:44.080
F-for starters, let me collect air from my idol's home.

08:44.080 --> 08:45.080
Don't do that.

08:47.750 --> 08:48.710
What?

08:48.710 --> 08:49.290
Huh?

08:49.290 --> 08:52.790
Oh, uh... DTM, was it?

08:55.630 --> 08:57.420
Don't stare around too much, okay?

09:04.880 --> 09:07.500
Hey, before we do anything else...

09:09.000 --> 09:12.080
...I think we need an icebreaker! Okay?

09:12.080 --> 09:14.420
Like I said, we're not here to enjoy ourselves.

09:14.750 --> 09:18.960
It's okay. This stuff is important
when you're working as a team.

09:21.250 --> 09:23.290
And that's not all.

09:23.290 --> 09:26.130
<b>Chocolate</b>

09:23.460 --> 09:24.330
Ta-daa!

09:24.960 --> 09:26.920
Ooh! Chocolate eggs!

09:27.170 --> 09:29.080
Here, each person gets one.

09:29.630 --> 09:31.920
You really love your sea creatures, huh?

09:32.630 --> 09:33.460
Ooh!

09:33.960 --> 09:35.960
What's this? A sea anemone?

09:35.960 --> 09:37.790
Aw, that's not a good one.

09:37.790 --> 09:38.380
My!

09:38.380 --> 09:40.080
They have good and bad ones?

09:42.420 --> 09:44.460
Oh! What's mine? An octopus?

09:44.630 --> 09:46.580
An octopus?! That's a good one!

09:46.880 --> 09:48.580
Uh, under what criteria?

09:50.460 --> 09:51.790
What did I get?

09:51.790 --> 09:52.420
Oh!

09:52.630 --> 09:54.130
A seahorse!

09:54.420 --> 09:55.250
Not a good one.

09:55.250 --> 09:56.790
But it seems like it'd be good!

09:57.290 --> 09:59.290
Seriously, what's your criteria?

10:00.080 --> 10:01.630
Let's see what I get.

10:02.250 --> 10:03.290
Wow!

10:03.540 --> 10:04.540
What is it?

10:04.830 --> 10:05.880
Here! Look!

10:06.580 --> 10:07.670
You got a jellyfish!

10:08.960 --> 10:11.130
But off course JELEE's illustrator would get that.

10:11.130 --> 10:12.540
Wow, it's like fate!

10:12.670 --> 10:14.580
You'd better treasure that.

10:15.380 --> 10:15.920
Huh?

10:16.420 --> 10:19.210
I'm glad I got this, but this is a team-building event.

10:19.460 --> 10:21.750
It can serve as a symbol that you're JELEE's leader.

10:23.130 --> 10:25.670
Uh, Kano? Do I see you blushing?

10:25.670 --> 10:30.040
Miss Mahiru, what are you implying?!
I refuse to make room for another fan!

10:31.750 --> 10:34.880
A dream, want to dream, it's not a dream

10:31.920 --> 10:34.080
My cheeks taste like peaches!

10:34.290 --> 10:38.130
I'm the sweetie of the Sunflower Dolls, Momoko Yanagi!

10:34.880 --> 10:37.710
Dance, drops, drops of sound

10:37.710 --> 10:41.290
Like tears, tears aren't so bad

10:38.630 --> 10:41.210
You're up next, Akarin.
Do you know how to introduce yourself?

10:41.790 --> 10:42.830
Hello!

10:42.500 --> 10:48.330
Hallelujah, write them over with light

10:42.830 --> 10:46.250
Uh, hey! I'm not a kid, okay?!

10:46.580 --> 10:48.250
I'm the Sunflower Dolls'...

10:48.250 --> 10:49.290
..."self-proclaimed"...

10:48.330 --> 10:51.420
And when that sky splits apart

10:49.290 --> 10:51.880
...sexy one, Akari Suzumura!

10:52.250 --> 10:55.460
Hey! Mr. Bando, I know I just caught your eye!

10:52.380 --> 10:54.420
love, weather

10:55.420 --> 10:56.630
lovely weather

10:55.460 --> 10:57.250
Lemme melt your heart!

10:56.630 --> 11:00.000
Everything surely is lovely weather

10:57.540 --> 11:01.630
I'm the dreamy one of the Sunflower Dolls, Mero Setou!

11:01.790 --> 11:03.920
You're all amazing for just being alive!

11:05.130 --> 11:07.290
Angels gave us ladders

11:05.420 --> 11:06.540
You girls keep it up!

11:08.420 --> 11:11.960
I see. I completely understand DTM now!

11:12.210 --> 11:13.380
Do you, though?

11:13.880 --> 11:14.920
You two done?

11:15.540 --> 11:17.830
Well, I taught her what I could.

11:17.830 --> 11:20.380
Okay, then let's talk scheduling!

11:21.500 --> 11:24.790
JELEE's ultimate goal is to get 100k followers!

11:25.130 --> 11:30.170
For starters, I would like to release
our next song by next Wednesday.

11:30.380 --> 11:31.000
Huh?

11:32.080 --> 11:32.790
Uh, what?

11:33.170 --> 11:37.170
So until we get that done,
I want us to get together every day.

11:37.540 --> 11:39.290
Every day, you say?

11:39.670 --> 11:43.540
Umm, we have to go back
to school the day after tomorrow.

11:43.790 --> 11:47.330
I know, but let's meet up in between all that!

11:47.330 --> 11:51.580
Hey, even I can tell that there's no way that's gonna work

11:51.920 --> 11:52.630
Huh?

11:52.960 --> 11:54.130
Wh-what about you, Mei?

11:54.330 --> 11:59.130
Nono-tan, I'm very sorry. I have
music lessons three times a week, so...

11:59.540 --> 12:01.630
But then what about the schedule?

12:01.920 --> 12:05.040
I mean, about this "schedule."

12:05.670 --> 12:08.000
You just went and decided that on your own, right?

12:08.460 --> 12:10.420
And why does it have to be Wednesday, anyway?

12:10.710 --> 12:11.880
Well...

12:12.790 --> 12:15.330
Th-the sooner the better, isn't it?

12:15.710 --> 12:21.330
Look, I have a bunch of other stuff I have to do too,
like streaming and video editing.

12:21.580 --> 12:23.580
It'll be even tougher for the two going to school.

12:23.830 --> 12:26.460
Won't the end of the month or something work?

12:26.880 --> 12:28.710
But we have it get it done on time.

12:28.710 --> 12:35.080
So I'm asking, what do you mean "on time"?
Why's the end of the month too late?

12:35.080 --> 12:36.830
What's your reasoning? Your source?

12:37.250 --> 12:38.210
Well...

12:39.130 --> 12:41.630
If you don't have a reason
you should listen to the rest of us.

12:41.920 --> 12:45.710
You don’t stand a chance arguing with
an undefeated flame war champion like me.

12:45.710 --> 12:48.880
You're totally the unreasonable one here,
Kano Yamanouchi.

12:49.420 --> 12:51.750
Kano, I understand how your feel,

12:52.170 --> 12:55.710
but all of us have things other than JELEE
we have to be doing, you know?

13:01.380 --> 13:04.540
Okay. I'm gonna go run to the convenience store.

13:04.540 --> 13:05.330
Nono-tan!

13:11.750 --> 13:13.000
What's up with her?

13:13.580 --> 13:15.540
Did I sound too harsh?

13:17.000 --> 13:17.710
Um.

13:18.210 --> 13:18.830
Hmm?

13:18.830 --> 13:21.170
She said next Wednesday, didn't she?

13:22.000 --> 13:26.710
<b>Here to perform their new song, "lovely weather."
The Sunflower Dolls</b>

13:22.290 --> 13:27.250
To kick off, we're releasing a double
A-side single next Wednesday!

13:27.960 --> 13:30.380
This will be the first time in two years
that the Sundolls release a song...

13:28.080 --> 13:29.380
I see.

13:30.630 --> 13:34.880
Well, if it's a rivalry thing I can kinda understand...

13:38.500 --> 13:39.380
Nono-tan?!

13:40.170 --> 13:46.460
Kano! My favorite host posted a photo with a
glimpse of another regular's nail art in-

13:46.460 --> 13:48.170
Uh, what?

13:54.460 --> 13:58.460
That's definitely Izu resort in the background, too!

13:58.750 --> 14:01.380
He only ever meets with me in Kabukicho!

14:01.380 --> 14:06.540
D-don't worry. I'm sure he's not actually betraying you.

14:08.000 --> 14:11.500
Pink girl... You're a great woman, you know that?

14:11.750 --> 14:12.710
Okay...

14:13.000 --> 14:14.710
So anyway, who are you all?

14:14.710 --> 14:15.750
Now you're asking us?

14:17.040 --> 14:18.790
Her friends, huh?

14:19.000 --> 14:22.000
I see, I see! So she finally made some.

14:26.170 --> 14:28.750
Hey, I'm her older sister, Mion.

14:29.130 --> 14:32.750
So? I don't see Kano around anywhere.

14:33.170 --> 14:33.960
Bathroom?

14:33.960 --> 14:37.250
No... We actually just got into an argument.

14:37.250 --> 14:39.420
What? She got in an argument?!

14:39.540 --> 14:41.710
U-um... excuse me!

14:41.710 --> 14:42.250
Hmm?

14:42.540 --> 14:46.960
Won't you please tell me what
I don't know about Nono-tan?

14:47.460 --> 14:48.880
I'd like to know as well!

14:50.210 --> 14:52.040
Ah, I get it.

14:52.500 --> 14:53.830
You're the ones.

14:53.830 --> 14:54.460
Huh?

14:54.710 --> 14:58.000
Sure, why not? I owe pink girl here one, anyway.

14:59.460 --> 15:04.170
My sister wasn't the one who said
she wanted to be an idol in the first place.

15:05.830 --> 15:09.580
Our parents got divorced when
we were in elementary school,

15:10.080 --> 15:12.880
and Kano became really attached to Mom ever since.

15:13.290 --> 15:15.920
She wanted to do whatever would please our mother.

15:16.460 --> 15:17.960
The opposite from me.

15:20.210 --> 15:21.330
Good evening, producer.

15:22.330 --> 15:25.420
Then you mean, the one who
applied to pop idol auditions...

15:26.080 --> 15:27.670
Focus on Mero a little longer.

15:30.790 --> 15:33.670
Well uh, that's not quite it.

15:34.130 --> 15:38.130
The producer of the Sunflower Dolls, Yukine Hayakawa.

15:38.130 --> 15:41.210
That's who our mother is, actually.

15:42.460 --> 15:43.540
The producer?

15:46.420 --> 15:51.380
So my sister was more diligent than anyone
and got results to show for it.

15:51.380 --> 15:54.210
But maybe because of that
she was isolated within the group,

15:54.500 --> 15:57.080
and then, there was that incident, right?

15:57.420 --> 16:00.290
The one where they say Kano punched a fellow member?

16:00.710 --> 16:04.670
Yeah. I never heard what drove her to do a thing like that.

16:05.000 --> 16:07.790
After she "retired" she came to live here.

16:07.790 --> 16:12.170
She spent everyday holed up in her room,
living off nothing but energy bars and soda.

16:12.500 --> 16:14.920
I told her she'd die if she kept that up!

16:16.460 --> 16:20.790
But she's been looking so much more alive these days.

16:20.790 --> 16:22.290
A lot more positive.

16:25.250 --> 16:27.080
Hey Sis, I can't believe it.

16:27.580 --> 16:28.380
Hngh?

16:28.540 --> 16:31.960
Lately, every day is just too fun!

16:32.380 --> 16:33.420
Huh?

16:39.710 --> 16:43.420
<b>Sunflower Dolls x Muraiya</b>

16:39.710 --> 16:43.420
<b>Chinese food & song tie-in pork buns</b>

16:39.830 --> 16:41.380
Just wow!

16:41.630 --> 16:43.460
They're sooo piping hot!

16:43.830 --> 16:45.920
Muraiya's Chinese pork buns!

16:47.210 --> 16:48.080
Mmm!

16:48.750 --> 16:50.750
So good!

16:52.170 --> 16:54.250
Piping hot Chinese pork buns!

16:55.290 --> 16:57.880
You should try them sometime!

17:03.580 --> 17:07.170
Man, I haven't changed at all.

17:13.630 --> 17:16.170
It can serve as a symbol that you're JELEE's leader.

17:19.420 --> 17:21.130
I can't get through to her.

17:21.130 --> 17:24.630
Hmm, do you have any leads?

17:25.540 --> 17:26.580
There's a mini gig.

17:27.920 --> 17:32.330
Later tonight, the Sundolls are performing
a live mini gig at Hanazono Shrine.

17:32.580 --> 17:33.630
She might be there.

17:34.920 --> 17:35.880
What's wrong?

17:36.290 --> 17:37.880
The venue's that way.

17:38.790 --> 17:43.290
A lonely person would find a lively place like that stifling.

17:43.790 --> 17:46.080
I'm guessing Kano's headed for somewhere more-

17:46.080 --> 17:47.710
That was such a long wait!

17:48.130 --> 17:49.130
Right?

17:50.540 --> 17:51.790
You don't suppose...

17:54.920 --> 17:55.880
Nono-tan!

17:56.210 --> 17:56.920
Huh?

18:01.170 --> 18:02.630
What were you doing?

18:02.960 --> 18:04.420
Uh, these are just...

18:06.000 --> 18:07.000
It was my bad.

18:07.000 --> 18:07.380
Huh?

18:07.830 --> 18:09.000
Here. Hand 'em over.

18:10.130 --> 18:12.960
And dude, why'dja get six? Who are they for?

18:13.330 --> 18:15.710
They had six flavors.

18:16.170 --> 18:17.880
And I didn't know which you'd all like.

18:18.580 --> 18:19.710
What are you, an idiot?

18:20.130 --> 18:21.210
Sh-shut up!

18:21.670 --> 18:23.040
Come on, let's go back.

18:23.330 --> 18:24.250
Okay.

18:25.670 --> 18:26.710
Where's Yoru?

18:27.500 --> 18:28.790
Welcome home!

18:32.880 --> 18:34.040
What? The room?

18:34.670 --> 18:37.960
I had some time on my hands
while the stew simmered, y'know?

18:39.130 --> 18:40.170
Thanks for this.

18:53.330 --> 18:55.130
I just sent you the drawing.

18:55.130 --> 18:56.040
Okay, thanks.

18:56.040 --> 18:58.330
Wow, it's amazing! It's lovely!

18:58.630 --> 18:59.920
I have to do a good job, too!

18:59.920 --> 19:01.000
Aww, thanks.

19:01.460 --> 19:03.080
What, are you smirking from that compliment?

19:03.080 --> 19:04.000
I am not!

19:04.000 --> 19:07.130
Don't you three have to go home soon?

19:07.500 --> 19:08.960
Oh, come on.

19:09.290 --> 19:10.000
Huh?

19:10.210 --> 19:13.790
We might not be able to get together
multiple times a week...

19:14.080 --> 19:15.880
...but let's give it our all tonight.

19:17.500 --> 19:19.210
You guys...!

19:22.130 --> 19:24.170
But why the sudden change of heart?

19:24.630 --> 19:28.630
Sorry, we actually heard a whole bunch about your past.

19:30.210 --> 19:32.830
I'm very sorry, I'm the one who asked.

19:32.830 --> 19:33.920
You know...

19:35.500 --> 19:38.380
I used to be the class superstar in elementary school,

19:39.170 --> 19:41.710
but my fall from grace after that was real pathetic.

19:42.130 --> 19:44.330
<b>KIUI WATASE</b>

19:42.210 --> 19:43.920
I'm the world's main event!

19:44.790 --> 19:46.540
And just like that I bombed my first day.

19:46.920 --> 19:50.540
That's when I knew life in middle school was so over.

19:50.960 --> 19:52.540
That's what happened?!

19:54.630 --> 19:55.500
Thanks.

19:56.790 --> 19:57.830
For what?

19:58.630 --> 20:01.290
Th-then I suppose it's my turn next.

20:01.670 --> 20:02.460
Mei?

20:03.080 --> 20:06.330
To be honest, I'm horrible at singing.

20:06.670 --> 20:09.130
Huh? But you're so good on the piano!

20:07.130 --> 20:10.290
Under the sunny spring sky

20:10.750 --> 20:13.580
on Sumida River...

20:11.040 --> 20:13.330
Miss Takanashi, you can stop there.

20:13.960 --> 20:14.790
All right.

20:15.920 --> 20:19.040
Even the teacher stopped me, and that was devastating.

20:19.380 --> 20:23.330
It felt like the world had decided
that I was the odd one out.

20:23.330 --> 20:24.750
I can kinda understand.

20:24.750 --> 20:28.000
Let's see, what about me, then?

20:28.000 --> 20:29.170
What? What?

20:29.420 --> 20:30.750
Actually...

20:30.880 --> 20:33.250
There's this person I'm kind of into right now.

20:33.460 --> 20:34.040
Huh?!

20:35.040 --> 20:35.750
What?!

20:35.960 --> 20:37.040
What kind of person?!

20:37.750 --> 20:38.420
Huh?

20:39.630 --> 20:45.920
"I'm home," I never managed to say
that properly. I found myself lost-

20:46.880 --> 20:49.580
Hey, can I change the lyrics here just a bit?

20:50.000 --> 20:52.960
Then I'd like to make this
part of the melody a lot brighter.

20:53.250 --> 20:55.540
Can you just send me what
you've finished recording for now?

20:56.000 --> 20:57.670
I really like this phrase.

20:58.000 --> 21:00.000
I want to draw another variation for this!

21:00.420 --> 21:05.210
Getting nowhere, I burst out into the empty city at night...

21:00.540 --> 21:02.630
I wanna go to Izu, too...

21:03.920 --> 21:06.000
Just one more drink, please...

21:05.540 --> 21:08.830
All alone I swim, dissolving into...

21:16.250 --> 21:20.210
<b>Drag and drop video files to upload</b>

21:16.250 --> 21:20.210
<b>Your videos will be private until you publish them
SELECT FILES</b>

21:19.250 --> 21:21.750
Okay, this is it, right?

21:22.130 --> 21:22.880
Yeah...

21:24.750 --> 21:27.630
<b>Back                     Publish</b>

21:29.500 --> 21:31.960
W...we're done!

21:31.960 --> 21:33.460
Yaaay...

21:35.080 --> 21:39.040
<b>[MV] The Moon's Warmth / JELEE
This is the second ever original music video from the anonymous artist JELEE!</b>

21:35.090 --> 21:39.040
<b>A song about telling someone something you never managed to say.</b>

21:48.880 --> 21:53.670
Karamawatte tobidashita dare mo inai yoru no machi

21:48.880 --> 21:53.670
Getting nowhere, I burst out into the empty city at night

21:53.670 --> 21:58.830
Hitoribocchi oyogunda kurayami ni toketeku

21:53.670 --> 21:58.830
All alone I swim, dissolving into the darkness

21:58.830 --> 22:03.540
Jibun katte wakatteru demo doushiyoumo nai hodo

21:58.830 --> 22:03.540
It's selfish, I know, but I can't help...

22:03.670 --> 22:08.750
Aserunda kowainda hikari kiete shimau no ga

22:03.670 --> 22:08.750
...how anxious, how scared I am that the light might disappear

22:09.040 --> 22:11.540
Doushite koko ni irundakke

22:09.040 --> 22:11.540
Why am I here again?

22:11.540 --> 22:13.880
Nani o sagashite itandakke

22:11.540 --> 22:13.880
What was I searching for again?

22:14.000 --> 22:19.000
Sorewa jihanki demo konbini demo uttenai mitai da

22:14.000 --> 22:19.000
No vending machine or convenience store seems to sell it, either

22:19.210 --> 22:21.580
Atatakai risou to tsumetai real

22:19.210 --> 22:21.580
A warm ideal and cold reality

22:21.580 --> 22:24.210
Moratta mono ga pocket ni aru

22:21.580 --> 22:24.210
In my pocket is the thing you gave me

22:24.210 --> 22:26.420
Toomawari shita kedo

22:24.210 --> 22:26.420
I went the long way round

22:26.670 --> 22:29.000
Kaeru beki basho e

22:26.670 --> 22:29.000
But it's back to where I belong

22:29.250 --> 22:33.330
Tsuki to te o tsunaide kaerou

22:29.250 --> 22:33.330
I'll go home with the moon, hand-in-hand

22:33.500 --> 22:38.540
Okaeri tte waratte kureta kimi ni

22:33.500 --> 22:38.540
"Welcome home," you said as you smiled

22:38.540 --> 22:43.580
Maigo no watashi o mitsukete kureta kimi ni

22:38.540 --> 22:43.580
You who found me when I was lost

22:43.580 --> 22:48.580
Chanto ietenai kotoba

22:43.580 --> 22:48.580
I never managed to tell you properly

22:48.580 --> 22:53.500
Atarimae nante omowanaide henji o shinakyana

22:48.580 --> 22:53.500
But I should reply without taking that for granted

22:53.670 --> 22:56.540
Tadaima tte

22:53.670 --> 22:56.540
And say, "I'm home"

22:58.670 --> 23:02.750
Arigatou tte

22:58.670 --> 23:02.750
And say, "Thanks"

23:04.960 --> 23:07.250
<b>The Moon's Warmth</b>

23:04.960 --> 23:07.250
<b>Kimura
Yoru Umitsuki
Nox Ryugasaki</b>

23:22.210 --> 23:23.130
Everyone!

23:23.460 --> 23:24.500
The reposts!

23:24.960 --> 23:26.420
The reposts!

